From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CBOC-Vita <344212538+CBOC-Vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:20:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 77/77] stability: file replace that works where rename refuses, ISO
 self-heal, power tick hook, audio underrun fade and cushion

- host/file_replace.hpp: rename; if the target exists and rename refuses, target -> .bak, temp -> target, delete .bak; recover()
  puts a .bak back when the target is missing. Used by savedata_store write_file (recovery on load/exists/write) and by the
  settings writer (which no longer removes the target first; load() also reads a .bak). Tests simulate a refusing rename.
- IsoImage::read reopens the file once and retries when a read comes up short; notify_resumed() reopens before the next read.
- KernelPlatform::power_tick: sceKernelPowerTick reaches the platform.
- AudioSink::pull fades the last sample to zero over 2 ms at a gap and fades the audio after it in; underruns (gaps under 250 ms)
  are counted and grow the restart margin by 20 ms up to 128 ms, which shrinks again after 30 s of calm.
  INFECTED_AUDIO_FADE=0 and INFECTED_AUDIO_CUSHION=0 switch them off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
